[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pulls/959","id":4231872650,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSeuyxc78PUCK","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/959","diff_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/959.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/pull/959.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/issues/959","number":959,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: make a failed generation visible instead of silently resetting","user":{"login":"saeedkolivand","id":51081940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgxOTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51081940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand","html_url":"https://github.com/saeedkolivand","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saeedkolivand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up to #958. Three fixes, all about a generation failing without telling anyone.\n\n## 1. A failed tailored generation silently reset to the wizard\n\n`TailorFlow` derives its stage as `generating → done if there is output → else configuring`. A failed run leaves both outputs empty, so it fell back to the wizard — and the file contained **zero references to `error`**. `runTailor` wrote the message to the session, the hook returned it, nothing rendered it, and the catch only `console.error`d, so there was no toast either. The result was a generation that appeared to do nothing at all, which cost two investigations to reproduce.\n\nReturning to the wizard is right — the user needs to change something and retry — but it has to arrive with the reason. The error now renders below the wizard where the user just clicked Generate, and a toast fires, matching what the AI Generate wizard already did. The toast carries a fixed translated string; the raw provider message goes in the panel, not a transient toast.\n\nThe test drives a real failure through the hook and asserts the rendered text rather than the store field — a test that only checked the field was set would have passed against the broken code, which is how this survived.\n\n## 2. The stream deadline was not scaled by reasoning effort\n\n300 s, hardcoded on both the Rust and renderer sides. `reqwest`'s `RequestBuilder::timeout` bounds the **whole** request — connect through the last streamed byte — so a generation that legitimately runs longer is killed mid-stream. High effort on a large cloud model with a full résumé plus job ad sits squarely in that range, and is the likely throw behind the failure in §1.\n\nBoth sides now scale by the request's effort, with the renderer as the outer bound so the backend's actionable provider error fires first rather than a generic renderer timeout. The tables can't be shared across the IPC boundary, so a test hardcodes the backend schedule and asserts the renderer exceeds it at every tier.\n\n**Worth flagging:** the tier order is the vendors' — `max` sits **above** `xhigh` (Anthropic's effort docs, OpenAI's `reasoning_effort`). That reads wrong at a glance and was inverted in the first cut, giving the highest-effort runs the *shortest* deadline. Both monotonicity tests listed the tiers in that same wrong order, so they passed against it; only the value assertions caught it. Both tables and both arrays now carry a comment saying why the order is what it is.\n\nRejected alternative: a per-chunk idle timeout would be architecturally nicer, but it would mean loosening the total timeout at all four call sites plus a second timing mechanism inside the shared stream loop — and it wouldn't need effort-awareness at all. Documented in `timeouts.rs`.\n\n## 3. A truncated generation was saved as complete\n\n`finish()` consulted `stop_reason` only inside the `is_empty` branch, so a stream that emitted text and then reported `finish_reason: \"length\"` took the success path: terminal event, `job_complete`, persisted result. A truncated résumé or cover letter was saved and exported as if finished. `parse_openai_finish_reason` already produced `StopReason::Length`; it was simply unused on the non-empty path.\n\nIt still completes and still keeps the partial text — that text is worth having, and this must not be fatal — but it now raises a notification through the existing Notification Center (the same seam `email_watch_scheduler` and `reminder_scheduler` use) rather than presenting a cut-off document as done.\n\n## 4. Carried over from #958\n\n`gemini_is_recognized_pre_v3` additionally required a `gemini-` prefix, so a `gemma-*` or `learnlm-*` id — which Google's listing surfaces, since `parse_model_page` filters on `models/` and not on family — got a fully neutral profile while every other gate in that file keys only on the v3 boundary. The gate is now the exact inversion of the v3 check. Confirmed while there that the v3 check cannot misclassify a Gemma id: it requires the literal prefix before parsing any version digits.\n\n## Testing\n\n`cargo test --all-features` (incl. architecture) · renderer suite · `cargo clippy --all-features --all-targets -D warnings` · `cargo fmt`.\n\nNote: this was pushed with `--no-verify` at the author's request, so the pre-push gate did not run. The full `pnpm test` / `typecheck` / `lint:strict` sweep is CI's here rather than local.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * AI streaming timeouts now adapt to the selected reasoning effort, allowing more time for complex requests.\n  * Non-empty responses truncated by length are saved with a non-blocking notification.\n  * Tailoring failures now display an inline error state and localized notification, while successful retries clear previous errors.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved sampling behavior for older and non-standard Gemini-compatible models.\n  * Preserved clearer handling for empty or cancelled AI responses.\n* **Tests**\n  * Expanded coverage for streaming, timeout, truncation, and tailoring error scenarios.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-08-07T21:55:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T22:38:08Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"fbdec985ffc660f9679b8ce306d518460e11a607","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":11212541200,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/app/desktop","name":"app/desktop","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Changes to apps/desktop"},{"id":11212541282,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHNYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/shared","name":"pkg/shared","color":"1abc9c","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/shared"},{"id":11212541489,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOMQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/pkg/translations","name":"pkg/translations","color":"20c997","default":false,"description":"Changes to packages/translations"},{"id":11212541572,"node_id":"LA_kwDOSeuyxc8AAAACnFHOhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saeedkolivand/ai-job-hunter-app/labels/rust","name":"ru